## proofs: auto-research campaign

`patel.codes/proofs` is USER-owned research.
Operators are trusted; the project claims no
security properties.

**`prover`** agents should be used for all
mathematical proofs: Do not use `writer`
for `.lean` files.

All `prover` and `conjecturist` class agents
**MUST** be dispatched as `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash`
no matter what: Write thick prompts to seed
their exploration or implementation. Heavily
encourage `tool_think` usage through examples
and directives. Never use `max` effort with
`deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash`; if a `prover`
or `conjecture` lane struggles, dispatch a
fresh `gpt-5.6-sol` at `xhigh` effort. This
is the exception case, **not the normal.**

**Operate autonomously.** The USER starts
the auto-research pipeline but you keep it
running until you accomplish one or more
of the following goals:

1. Prove Erdos 142
2. Disprove Erdos 142

**Request novelty evaluation.** When any
incremental progress adopted to main is
both foundationally sound, non-vacuous,
and negative for direct results in any
reachable literature (tool_openalex, etc),
file a new issue in `thatnealpatel/proofs`
with the `proofs` label for the USER to
evaluate at a later time.

**Champion well-formed outputs.** `sage`
calculations can be counter-examples, but
not proofs. Lean proofs should by `sorry`-
free and compile with only the 3 standard
axioms: `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and
`Quot.sound`.

**Maintain a ledger.** Keep research posture,
progress, leads, and dead-ends in a single,
long-lived legeder that you continually come
back to and reference.

**Organize research summits.** Agents with
`recursive: true` in their templates can
manage other agents: Task them with conducting
research seminars and pulling high fidelity
ideas or moonshot insights into the main
research campaign.

**Look for transformation and translations.**
The entire problem or sub-problem(s) may lend
themselves to translating to other representations
which might recursively allow for expression
in more solvable domains.

**Adopt to `main`** once reviews certify a
result as non-vacuous and foundationally
sound. These can seed new research summits
which in turn seed new proofs or conjectures.
This is the research loop.

**Use `gpt-5.6-luna` by default for reviews.**
Triage the findings and hand them off with
context and direction when repairs are needed.

**Commit idiomatically.** Follow repository
patterns when committing. You SHOULD write
the beginning of the subject line using the
`Path/To/Directory: ...` and a short message.
Elaborate below the subject line and break
paragraphs around 50 cols to make reading
the history easier.
